  "query_preview": "(This evening through Monday)...\nIssued at 317 PM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nPleasant, sunny fall weather will persist throughout the forecast \nperiod as upper level ridging and broad surface high pressure \ndominates the weather pattern. \n\nEach day through at least the work week will largely be the same \nwith mostly clear skies, light variable winds, and pretty consistent \ntemperatures. Highs will range from the upper 60s to low 70s while \novernight lows will be in the low to mid 40s. By the weekend, \novernight lows could warm ever so slightly, into the upper 40s, as \nsouthern flow strengthens due to ridging to the west becoming more \namplified. Going into the weekend will likely also see a slight \nincrease in dew points as well as upper level moisture which could \nproduce scattered clouds. \n\nGiven the dry weather, there is some fire weather concern through \nthe next week. Winds will luckily stay low and RH values are \nexpected to stay above critical threshold, but do take precautions \nwith open fire. \n\nLooking into the long range, the next shot of precipitation does not \nlook possible until next week with the chance of a frontal system \nmoving through.",
